      "text": "## The Big Picture: Immunopathology Is Friendly Fire — a Defense System Injuring Its Own Host"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-IMMUNOPATHOLOGY-AND-TISSUE-INJURY.md#007",
      "path": [
        "04-IMMUNOPATHOLOGY-AND-TISSUE-INJURY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:pathology:04-immunopathology-and-tissue-injury]",
        "canonical_path": "pathology/04-IMMUNOPATHOLOGY-AND-TISSUE-INJURY.md",
        "concepts": "[hypersensitivity, autoimmunity, transplant-rejection, immunodeficiency-lesion, amyloid-deposition]",
        "current_path": "pathology/04-IMMUNOPATHOLOGY-AND-TISSUE-INJURY.md",
        "id": "maxim:pathology:immunopathology-and-tissue-injury",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "pathology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[immunopathology]",
        "section": "pathology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Immunopathology and Tissue Injury",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The novice mental model is \"the immune system fights infection; sometimes it's weak.\" The\nexpert model is that the immune system is a **powerful weapons platform** whose whole job is to\ndestroy targets, and immunopathology is the study of **that platform injuring the host** — by\nfiring at the *wrong target* (autoimmunity), *too hard* at a harmless target\n(hypersensitivity), at a *foreign but medically desirable* target (transplant rejection), or\nby being *unable to fire* so that opportunists injure the tissue instead (immunodeficiency).\nThe unifying insight is that the *effector mechanisms are the same ones that protect* — this\nguide is the pathology of defense turned against the tissue it defends."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-IMMUNOPATHOLOGY-AND-TISSUE-INJURY.md#008",
      "path": [
        "04-IMMUNOPATHOLOGY-AND-TISSUE-INJURY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:pathology:04-immunopathology-and-tissue-injury]",
        "canonical_path": "pathology/04-IMMUNOPATHOLOGY-AND-TISSUE-INJURY.md",
        "concepts": "[hypersensitivity, autoimmunity, transplant-rejection, immunodeficiency-lesion, amyloid-deposition]",
        "current_path": "pathology/04-IMMUNOPATHOLOGY-AND-TISSUE-INJURY.md",
        "id": "maxim:pathology:immunopathology-and-tissue-injury",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "pathology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[immunopathology]",
        "section": "pathology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Immunopathology and Tissue Injury",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nTHE FOUR FAILURE MODES OF IMMUNITY  (this guide owns the tissue injury each causes)\n==================================================================================\n  WRONG TARGET        AUTOIMMUNITY        immune attack on SELF antigens\n        |                                 (tolerance is lost)\n  TOO HARD            HYPERSENSITIVITY    excessive/inappropriate response to an\n        |                                 antigen (self, environmental, or microbial)\n  FOREIGN-BUT-WANTED  TRANSPLANT REJECT.  attack on a grafted tissue (alloimmunity);\n        |                                 GVHD is the mirror image\n  CANNOT FIRE         IMMUNODEFICIENCY    defense fails -> opportunists + unusual\n                                          lesions injure the tissue instead\n  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  COMMON THREAD: the EFFECTOR mechanisms (antibody, complement, T cells,\n  phagocytes) are the SAME weapons that protect. Injury = the weapon + a\n  target it should not be destroying (or the absence of the weapon).\n```"
    },
