        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Immunopathology and Tissue Injury",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Two facts organize the guide. First, **the type of injury is set by the effector, not the\ntrigger**: the same antigen can cause different lesions depending on whether antibody,\nimmune complexes, or T cells do the damage — which is exactly what the Gell and Coombs\nclassification captures. Second, this guide **stops at the tissue-injury mechanism**: it owns\n*how the immune response damages tissue and what that damage looks like*, and hands the biology\nof the immune cells to `immunology/` and the specific diseases to `disease/`."
    }
